# The OAuth App that "Sign in with GitHub" authorizes against.
#
# Not a secret: the Device Flow has no client secret, and this value is
# readable in any shipped binary. It is kept out of the repository because,
# published, it lets anyone raise a GitHub consent screen carrying this
# app's name, and it shares this app's rate limits and org approvals.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill it in, or export the variable
# before building. Without it the app still works: Settings takes a client
# id, and the GitHub CLI's token needs none at all.
DEEP_REVIEW_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
